  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1... \nScattered lake effect rain showers and isolated thunder will\ncontinue to impact the \"Snowbelt\" area of far Northeast Ohio and\nNorthwest Pennsylvania today through tonight. A deep upper \nlevel trough has developed over the eastern half of the Great \nLakes this morning and will slowly move eastward by tomorrow.\nThe backside of this trough will continue to bring a cooler \nnortherly flow over the eastern Great Lakes today and tonight \nbefore it finally pulls away Tuesday. Therefore, scattered lake\neffect rain showers will continue over NEOH and NWPA through \nearly Tuesday morning. Rain chances or POPS will be likely today\nand gradually decrease overnight into early Tuesday morning. \n\nFor the rest of northern and central Ohio, nicer weather will\nreturn today with mostly sunny to partly cloudy skies and drier\nweather. High pressure will build across the Ohio Valley today\nand continue to bring very nice weather through Wednesday.\nHigh temperatures will be cooler today with upper 60s in far \nNEOH and NWPA where there will be more clouds and showers from\nlake effect. North central and Northwest Ohio will have more\nsunshine with passing scattered clouds and high temps in the\nlower to middle 70s. It will also feel less humid with the drier\nairmass moving. High temps will slowly climb over the next few\ndays reaching the upper 70s to lower 80s on Wednesday areawide.\nOvernight low temps will be in the 50s away from the immediate\nlakeshore. \n\n\nKEY MESSAGE 2.. \nThe next chance for showers and thunderstorms will be Wednesday\nnight through Thursday evening with a weak, slow moving cold\nfront across the Great Lakes region. The latest model guidance\nhas trended slightly downward on POPs and QPF. At this time, it\nappears there will be scattered showers and some thunder \npossible with the greater POPs around 40 to 50 percent during\nday Thursday. Severe weather is not expected at this as\nthe thermodynamics looks fairly weak. High pressure will build\nback into the region on Friday with warm and nice day. High\ntemperatures will climb through next weekend with lower to \nmiddle 80s across the area.",
